    "head_commit_message": "fix(ci): github-sync closes a built step's issue against the PR that built it\n\nA step split while it was built (7b) only gets its heading under the\nspec's Built section in its own PR, so the sync makes its issue after that\nPR merges. The PR carries the parent step's label, so the rule that\ncreates a merged step closed missed it, and the issue stayed open (#604,\n#598). A step whose headings all sit under Built is now closed as\ncompleted against the PR whose merge first added its heading, found with\ngit log -S, with a comment naming it. Headings under Steps are never\nclosed this way. The workflow fetches the whole history for it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SbQA1BnZdXSYjceCQLTk19",
